---
/**
 * The step between the 30-second cut and the <ReadInDetail> curtain.
 *
 * It used to draw a rule here as well, matching the one StorySection's
 * `divider` puts under the hero. That rule is gone deliberately — don't add it
 * back: the curtain's own wash already announces the break, and a hairline
 * directly above it read as a second, competing divider.
 *
 * What remains is the gap, which is still load-bearing. The py-20 stacks with
 * the preceding section's own py-20 and .read-more's padding-block-start:
 * ~288px of air before the CTA. That is the spacing the pages already shipped
 * with, so it is preserved rather than quietly retuned — change it once, here,
 * if the gap wants closing.
 *
 * A component rather than a div in each MDX file: the case studies were
 * carrying byte-identical copies of this markup, complete with a hardcoded
 * `border-neutral-800` that is invisible on the light ground — a colour
 * literal in content, where no component-level fix can reach it. Keeping it a
 * component is also why removing the rule was one edit rather than three.
 */
---

<div class="mx-auto max-w-[var(--measure-story)] px-[var(--gutter)] py-20"></div>
